{
  "requires": "reader-routing",
  "note": "Phase 3a owns the reader but not the routing that reaches it: AppShell still shows the Phase 1 placeholder in the Quran tab until Phase 3e wires ReaderView.screen(for:). This spec is therefore wrapped in an envelope rather than written at the top level, so LayoutSpecTests' loader (which decodes every JSON in the UI test bundle as a bare LayoutSpec) skips it instead of failing against the placeholder. ReaderTests unwraps it and skips itself, with a message, until the route is live. The frames were recorded with SCROLL_RECORD_SPECS=1 from ReaderView running on ScrollSim-3a and checked against Reference/reader-dark.png. They are XCUITest *accessibility* frames: for a text element that is the union of its glyph boxes and for a control it includes the tap padding, so it is not always the visual box. Elements whose box is content-driven (the page container, the verse block, the reference line) are asserted for existence only; the chrome, which is the layout this screen has to hold, is asserted by frame.",
